WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.746 --> 00:00:12.496
You know, there are very few things that
set us apart

00:00:12.496 --> 00:00:14.454
from the rest of life on Earth.

00:00:15.204 --> 00:00:21.079
At the heart of them, I believe, is our 
inexhaustible power of imagination.

00:00:23.746 --> 00:00:27.454
Imagination is the ability to bring 
into mind, things that aren’t present.

00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:31.621
With imagination, we can
anticipate the future.

00:00:34.662 --> 00:00:36.121
We can revisit the past.

00:00:38.746 --> 00:00:40.871
You can step outside the present moment

00:00:40.871 --> 00:00:43.079
and try and see things 
as other people see them.

00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:48.204
It’s through creativity that we develop
our architecture,

00:00:49.537 --> 00:00:50.912
our scientific proofs,

00:00:52.371 --> 00:00:53.704
and our works of art.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.746
We don’t just
live in the world as we find it,

00:00:56.746 --> 00:01:01.371
we create civilizations, theories,
technologies,

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:06.079
and we reach beyond the planet.

00:01:08.163 --> 00:01:11.371
In honor of the life and work
of Sir Ken Robinson,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:16.454
TED-Ed invites you to reimagine 
the aspects of life we take for granted

00:01:16.454 --> 00:01:20.538
by finishing the sentence: 
imagine if ...

00:01:21.954 --> 00:01:27.746
Visit ed.ted.com/ImagineIf
to learn more.

